Everyone shares ONE depot. There is no private inventory, no slot or file system.
All raw resources are supplied at round start, in finite quantities. There is no
get, deposit, withdraw, delete, transfer, trade, or way to replenish resources.
Nothing moves between agents: an item is either in the shared depot or consumed.

OPERATIONS
- act("craft ..."): run one recipe copied exactly; it consumes the inputs and adds the full output, e.g. 'craft 2 b using 1 a' turns 1 a into 2 b. Costs one action, even when inputs are short or the command is invalid.
{% if craft_duration_s %}  Each accepted craft takes {{ craft_duration_s | round | int }} seconds. Its inputs leave the depot when it starts and its output lands when it ends; until then you can do nothing else, while teammates keep working.
{% endif %}{% if uncraft_enabled %}- act("uncraft craft ..."): undo one earlier craft of that recipe while its full output is still in the depot; the output is removed and every input, raw materials included, comes back. Costs one action.
{% endif %}{% if comms_enabled %}- observe(): see the current depot and new messages. Free.
- wait_for_message(): pause until a teammate's message arrives. Free.
- send(text): message your teammates. Costs no action.
{% else %}- observe(): see the current depot. Free.
{% endif %}- finish(): stop for the rest of the round. Free.
Any crafter may run any recipe{% if recipe_holders %} whose exact command it has{% endif %}. Calls that compete for the same inputs run one at a time, so the later one can fail.

